<title>CHILE: Chile cenbank sells option to HSBC.</title>
<headline>Chile cenbank sells option to HSBC.</headline>
<dateline>SANTIAGO 1997-07-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Chile's central bank said it has agreed to sell its option to buy shares in Banco Santiago's forthcoming capital increase to HSBC Holdings Plc for $14.5 million.</p>
<p>&quot;With this deal HSBC, once it has exercised its option, will own approximately seven percent,&quot; said the bank in a statement.</p>
<p>HSBC already owns 3.9 percent of Banco Santiago, Chile's largest private bank.</p>
</text>
